error[X0526]: a `constexpr` function must be `static`
 --> constexpr.xn:5:10
  |
5 |   public constexpr function notStatic(n:int):int => n                        // must be static
  |          ^^^^^^^^^
  |
help: it can only use its parameters: add `static`

error[X0526]: a `constexpr` function has an expression body
 --> constexpr.xn:6:17
  |
6 |   public static constexpr function block(n:int):int { return n }             // needs an expression body
  |                 ^^^^^^^^^
  |
help: write it as `=> expression`

error[X0526]: `constexpr` is for functions
 --> constexpr.xn:7:17
  |
7 |   public static constexpr LIMIT:int = 10                                     // constants are `inline final`
  |                 ^^^^^^^^^ not a function
  |
help: a compile-time constant is `inline final`: `static inline final LIMIT:…`

error[X0526]: `counter` isn't allowed in a `constexpr` function
 --> constexpr.xn:8:63
  |
8 |   public static constexpr function useField(n:int):int => n + counter        // not a constant
  |                 ---------                                     ^^^^^^^ not a parameter or an inline constant
  |                 |
  |                 `constexpr` here
  |
  = note: allowed: parameters, literals, operators, `?:`, conversions like `int()`, inline constants, `Math` functions and other `constexpr` functions

